{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "095S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y \\cap Z = Y \\times_{\\Spec(A)} \\Spec(A/I)$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$Z$", "MATH_0008": "$X \\to \\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0011": "$(B, IB)$", "MATH_0012": "$X \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0013": "$T \\subset \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$X$", "MATH_0016": "$A$", "MATH_0017": "$T \\cap V(I)$", "MATH_0018": "$Y \\times_{\\Spec(A)} \\Spec(A/I) \\to T \\cap V(I)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-h0-topological}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-quasi-compact-quasi-separated-spectral}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-theorem-stein-factorization-general}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-integral-over-henselian-pair}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-irreducible-henselian-pair-connected}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{topology-lemma-connected-fibres-quotient-topology-connected-components}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34f0b4d4bbc5a45982d22b65142e2877d581191b53d173f1177d8ed0df74ba2e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:94a0f448d9a694c229a44c8722e3132fe820f8ed0adf84081dd601865b371f0b", "source_text": "We will use Lemma <REF_0001> to prove this. First observe\nthat the underlying topological space of <MATH_0001> is spectral by Properties, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an irreducible closed subscheme. To finish the proof\nwe show that <MATH_0003> is connected.\nReplacing <MATH_0004> by <MATH_0005>\nwe may assume that <MATH_0006> is irreducible and we have to show that <MATH_0007>\nis connected. Let <MATH_0008> be the Stein factorization\nof <MATH_0009> (More on Morphisms, Theorem\n<REF_0003>).\nThen <MATH_0010> is integral and <MATH_0011> is a henselian pair\n(More on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nThus we may assume the fibres of <MATH_0012> are geometrically\nconnected. On the other hand, the image <MATH_0013> of <MATH_0014>\nis irreducible and closed as <MATH_0015> is proper over <MATH_0016>. Hence <MATH_0017>\nis connected by More on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0005>.\nNow <MATH_0018>\nis a surjective closed map with connected fibres.\nThe result now follows from Topology, Lemma\n<REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f7133fe869bf48209f750dd5111e3048ecc241e2af2ed99c910c086afb6c087", "unit_id": "tag:0A0B:proof"}
